.TH BOSWAS-PRESET 1 "November 2026" "boswas-branding 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-preset \- list and switch the Boswas OS desktop presets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B list
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B current
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B apply
.I PRESET
.RB [ \-\-layout ]
.br
.B boswas-preset
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.B reset
.SH DESCRIPTION
Boswas OS ships ten presets of one design system: Horizon (the default),
Midnight, Aurora, Slate, Carbon, Pearl, Ocean, Ember, Nebula and Classic.
Each brings a colour scheme, light, dark and lock-screen wallpapers, a
Konsole profile, and a Plasma Global Theme with a panel layout.
.PP
On the native Boswas desktop
.RB ( boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-shell (1))
a preset sets light or dark for the shell and the window frames, the
wallpaper, the colours of KDE applications and the Konsole profile. The
accent colour of the shell, the icon theme, the panel and the lock-screen
background do not change. A user who has not applied a preset has the
Boswas Prism look, which is not one of the ten.
.PP
On a KDE Plasma session a preset applies its Global Theme, wallpaper,
lock-screen wallpaper and Konsole profile.
.PP
Boswas Control Center (Personalization) uses this command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
The presets with their identifier, name, description, light or dark variant
and accent colour, and the current preset.
.TP
.B current
The preset in use (the recorded choice, otherwise the active Global Theme
of a Plasma session). Nothing is printed when no preset has been applied.
.TP
.BI apply " PRESET"
Apply a preset for the signed-in user. On the native Boswas desktop
(\fBXDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP\fR contains \fBBoswas\fR) this writes
.IR ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml ,
merges the preset's colours into
.IR ~/.config/kdeglobals ,
sets the Konsole default profile and asks the running compositor to reload
its configuration. On a Plasma session it applies the Global Theme, the
desktop wallpaper, the lock-screen wallpaper and the Konsole default
profile. With
.BR \-\-layout ,
a Plasma session's panels are also replaced with the preset's layout (your
own panel changes are lost); the native desktop has one panel layout and
ignores the option. Runs as the desktop user; refused for root.
.TP
.B reset
Return to the default look. On the native Boswas desktop that is Boswas
Prism, which is no preset: the command removes
.IR ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml ,
merges the Boswas Prism colours into
.IR ~/.config/kdeglobals ,
makes "Boswas Prism" the Konsole default profile, clears the recorded
preset and asks the running compositor to reload. On a Plasma session it
applies the Horizon preset with its panel layout. Runs as the desktop user;
refused for root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 a step failed (the message names it), 2 unknown preset,
3 usage error, 4 run as root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/boswas/presets/presets.json
The preset definitions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswasrc
The recorded choice ([Preset] Current).
.TP
.I ~/.config/boswas/appearance.toml
Native desktop: light or dark and the wallpaper, read by
.BR boswas-compositor (1).
Rewritten as a whole by every
.BR apply .
.TP
.I ~/.config/kdeglobals
Native desktop: the colours of KDE applications. Only the colour groups
and the ColorScheme entry are replaced.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR boswas-compositor (1),
.BR boswas-control-center (1)
